            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for the paramedic, then the German for the emergency room."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: warnen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "warnen — \"to warn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Die Nachbarin warnte uns vor dem Hund. The neighbour warned us about the dog."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Vor etwas warnen — to warn about something. Die Warnung — the warning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "warnen is inherited from Middle High German warnen \"to watch over, to protect\" (EtymDB), a cousin of English warn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
